@media (min-width: 901px) { html body main.layout .listing-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr)) !important; } }

/* WAVE 180b — rail/grid cards: let the price row (price + steam + discount badge) WRAP on narrow cards instead of clipping at the card edge (operator screenshot: "-18%" half-cut on home rail at ~200px cards). Wrapping only engages when the row cannot fit. */
html body .grid-card .grid-price { flex-wrap: wrap !important; row-gap: 2px !important; }

/* WAVE 180c — operator screenshot: a TRANSPARENT sticky-bottom pager floated over /db table rows (sticky from rule ~23259, transparent bg from the higher-specificity ~22589 duel). The page itself is the scroller in full-page-mode, so sticky pins to the viewport and covers data rows. Return the pager to normal flow at the end of the table. */
html body .db-pager { position: static !important; box-shadow: none !important; backdrop-filter: none !important; -webkit-backdrop-filter: none !important; }

/* WAVE 180d — operator: "when I click something the menu disappears." On every full-page-mode route (db/profile/wallet/cart/...) the opaque .modal-backdrop (z-index 200) sat ON TOP of the sticky nav (z-index 50): the nav was buried under the backdrop — invisible and unclickable, so there was no way to navigate off these pages. Drop the backdrop below the nav and pad its scroller so content clears the bar. Desktop-scoped; the mobile layering already shows the nav. */
@media (min-width: 901px) { html body .site-root.full-page-mode .modal-backdrop { z-index: 40 !important; padding-top: 70px !important; box-sizing: border-box !important; } }

/* WAVE 181 — operator: item page read as scattered widgets in a void. (1) .modal-preview was hard-capped at 760px inside its 1064px grid column, leaving a ~300px dead strip mid-page and stranding the rarity badge at the box corner far from the artwork — preview now fills its column (one intentional media panel) with the badge pinned to the panel's top-left. (2) The four stat boxes (listing price / steam ref / 30d change / supply) were separate floating cards — merged into ONE panel with internal row dividers. Desktop-scoped. */
