   to its buttons: the panel is overflow:hidden and the backdrop does not scroll. Cap it to the screen and let it scroll. */
html body .cart-confirm-backdrop > .cart-confirm-panel { max-height: calc(100dvh - 4vh) !important; overflow-y: auto !important; overscroll-behavior: contain; }
/* Phones: Cancel + a long primary ("Save trade URL & buy · $0.67") were wider than the panel, and with flex-end the Cancel button
   was pushed off the left edge. Let the row wrap and the buttons share the width. */
@media (max-width: 480px) {
  html body .cart-confirm-panel .cart-confirm-actions { flex-wrap: wrap !important; }
  html body .cart-confirm-panel .cart-confirm-actions > .btn { flex: 1 1 auto !important; }
}
/* Desktop full-page routes (profile, db, cart, stall, offers...) scroll inside a fixed backdrop padded for a nav at the
   very top. With the email-confirm or a site announcement banner above the nav, the backdrop hid the banner and the
   nav sat over each page's heading. Let those pages flow under the banner and nav instead. */
@media (min-width: 901px) {
  html body .site-root.full-page-mode:has(> .announce-banner) .modal-backdrop { position: static !important; padding: 0 0 36px !important; }
}
/* Stall recent sales carry the item name as a fourth cell. The three-column sales-log grid pushed the time onto a
   second line that spilled over the next row. */
html body .stall-recent-sales .recent-sales-list .recent-sales-row { grid-template-columns: 76px minmax(0, 1fr) auto auto !important; }
/* Stall section heads hold only a dot and a title; space-between threw the title to the far right. */
html body .stall-reviews-head, html body .stall-review-cta-head { justify-content: flex-start !important; gap: 8px !important; }
/* Stall "Leave a review": the comment box shares the review-body class (no box, no width) and sat as a two-line
   sliver beside 14px stars; the two-cell trade rows sat in a three-column grid that squeezed the item name to 40px. */
.stall-review-form { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; }
html body .stall-review-form textarea.stall-review-text { width: 100% !important; min-height: 88px; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 10px 12px !important; margin: 0 !important; background: var(--bg-2); border: 1px solid var(--line-2); border-radius: 8px; color: var(--ink); font: inherit; resize: vertical; }
html body .stall-review-form .stall-review-stars-picker button { font-size: 22px !important; }
html body .stall-review-cta-row { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto !important; }
/* Staff panels: the modal-wide CTA rule (full width, 320px, 18px top margin) also caught the buttons that sit in a
   row beside an input (Users/CSR search, ticket Send, Goodwill) and squeezed the input to a 22px sliver on phones. */
.info-modal:has(.staff-banner) .info-modal-body [style*="display: flex"] > .btn.btn-accent { width: auto !important; max-width: none !important; margin: 0 !important; flex: 0 0 auto; }
/* CSR lookup card stacks its sections; the three-column grid put the whole header row into a 56px column. */
.csr-user-card { display: block; }
.csr-tx-row { grid-template-columns: auto minmax(0, 1fr) auto; }
/* Staff banner on phones: the bold "ADMIN MODE" label stood as its own narrow column beside the sentence. */
@media (max-width: 600px) { html body .staff-banner, html body .staff-banner.csr { display: block !important; text-align: center !important; } }
/* Profile > Trades opens Confirm receipt and Leave review in their own backdrop inside the full-page profile, and the
   full-page rule made that backdrop static too: the dialog sat in the page flow under the trade list, off screen. */
html body .site-root.full-page-mode .modal-backdrop .modal-backdrop { position: fixed !important; inset: 0 !important; z-index: 200 !important; display: grid !important; place-items: center !important; padding: 4vh 16px !important; overflow-y: auto !important; background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.55) !important; }
html body .site-root.full-page-mode .modal-backdrop .modal-backdrop > .modal { width: 100% !important; max-width: 480px !important; }
